    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Woodstock was officially platted in September 1879, marking the start of its development as a rural community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodstock%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Shortly after the Saint Paul and Sioux City Railroad extended its line to the area in 1878, Woodstock was platted, enabling agricultural transport.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/woodstock_minnesota",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Early development focused on homes, stores, and grain elevators, with agriculture driving economic activity and Catholic missions serving settlers by the early 1880s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/woodstock_minnesota",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The region's glacial till and outwash plains offer well-drained soils, yet intermittent streams make the area vulnerable to erosion and flooding, shaping land use.",
